// Micro-benchmark: a `state` hit inside a function. `counter` is called from
// a 200-iteration loop, so its declaration holds 200 slots, one per call path
// (loop index, callsite), and each call after the first run is a hit. See
// state_hit_top.ptl for the command; the control is state_hit_none.ptl.

fn counter(i)
  state n = i
  n
end

var sum = 0
for i in range(0, 200) do
  set sum = sum + counter(i)
end
sum
